{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading","kind":"remark","title":"Localized knots and hadrons under the knot–particle bijection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-knot-particle-correspondence","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hadron"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-knot-particle-correspondence","tags":["knot","particle","dictionary","hadron","markov-trace"],"text":"knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading\"></a><p>In particular, each localized knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(p, K)</code> in a bundle corresponds to a unique irreducible summand. Hadrons correspond to tensor products of such summands bound by Hopf links.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/knot-particle-correspondence-hadron-reading.md","heading":"Remark","number":"9.4.7"}
